+msgid "Without a password, anyone on your home network can open, change and delete what is in the shares of this system: your videos and music, the drives you plug in, the backups, the settings of Kodi and of its add-ons (with the accounts and keys they keep), and the folder of start-up scripts, which run as root. LibreELEC shares this way; LibreELEC Hades asks for a password by default.[CR][CR]Windows 11 (version 24H2 and later) refuses such a share by default too.[CR][CR]Share without a password?"
